@startuml "Command - Account (Solution) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title The teller, with each request an object

class Teller <<Invoker>> {
  - done : Deque<Transaction>
  - undone : Deque<Transaction>
  + perform(Transaction)
  + undo()
  + redo()
  + journal() : List<String>
}

interface Transaction <<Command>> {
  + execute()
  + undo()
  + description() : String
}

class Deposit <<ConcreteCommand>>
class Withdraw <<ConcreteCommand>>
class CloseOut <<ConcreteCommand>> {
  - taken : Money
}
class Transfer <<ConcreteCommand>> {
  - steps : List<Transaction>
}

class Account <<Receiver>> {
  + balance() : Money
  + deposit(Money)
  + withdraw(Money)
}

class StandingOrders {
  - tonight : Queue<Transaction>
  + schedule(Transaction)
  + runThrough(Teller)
}

Teller o--> "*" Transaction
StandingOrders o--> "*" Transaction
Transaction <|.. Deposit
Transaction <|.. Withdraw
Transaction <|.. CloseOut
Transaction <|.. Transfer
Transfer o--> "2" Transaction
Deposit --> Account
Withdraw --> Account
CloseOut --> Account

note right of Teller
  <b>No switch, no case, no operation named.</b>
  Undo takes the last transaction off the
  pile and asks it to undo itself.
end note

note bottom of CloseOut
  <b>Remembers what it took.</b>
  The request had no amount;
  undo needs the one it found.
end note

note bottom of Transfer
  <b>One object on the history.</b>
  A withdrawal and a deposit,
  undone together, in reverse.
end note
@enduml
